<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Simple Prayer — the Wear OS watch face (Milestone V, V6b).
  Direction A "Manuscript", owner-picked from the WatchFace design canvas;
  the canvas is drawn at 450x450 and its pixel numbers are used here 1:1.

  Palette: the night-paper tokens from src/theme/tokens.ts, as literal ARGB hex (Watch Face
  Format is resource-only XML; no code, so no imports):
    bg #20190e (in the vignette PNG) · ink #ece0c4 · inkStrong #dcb96f · faint #9c8a60
    muted #ad9a6e · soft #93805a · accent #bf9950 · diamond #cba85e
    track rgba(214,180,110,0.25) = #40d6b46e · hairline rgba(214,180,110,0.34) = #57d6b46e
    ambient arc rgba(191,153,80,0.28) = #47bf9950 · ambient diamond rgba(203,168,94,0.7) = #b3cba85e

  Live data arrives through two complication slots locked to the app's own data source
  (app.simpleprayer.wear.PrayerComplicationService, built in V6a):
    slot 1 SHORT_TEXT   — "Asr · 1:12"-class next-prayer line (TITLE · TEXT)
    slot 2 RANGED_VALUE — progress through the current prayer window (the ring), whose TEXT,
                          when the provider fills it, renders as the "until 6:42 pm" line
  The countdown is therefore computed by the system from the complication's data, never a
  pushed string that goes stale.

  Ambient (AOD) follows the canvas's "A, always-on" frame: near-black ground, single gold,
  time + one prayer line + the arc at reduced alpha; no seconds, no texture, no vignette.
  The five-seal micro-row from the interactive canvas is a face SETTING in the design sheet;
  v1 omits it (five independent statuses don't fit the complication slots this face spends).

  ═══ ARABIC: ONE FACE, TWO FONT RESOURCES (AR-14, fixed 2026-08-30) ═══════════════════════

  Every <Font family=…> below names face_regular or face_semibold, and those resolve per SYSTEM
  LOCALE: res/font/ holds Lora, res/font-ar/ holds Noto Naskh Arabic 400/600 (D135's UI face —
  these are 20–30sp UI lines, not calligraphy, and slot 1 asks for SemiBold, a weight Amiri does
  not ship). One watchface.xml serves every language; there is no res/raw-ar/ to drift.

  Why the families are named for their ROLE and not their typeface: it is the only way a single
  layout can hand each locale a face that can draw it. Verified in the built APK, not assumed —
  `aapt2 dump resources` reports font/face_regular with two configs, `()` and `(ar)`.

  WHAT THE ARABIC EMULATOR PASS FOUND (Wear_OS_Large_Round booted `-prop persist.sys.locale=ar-SA`,
  config `ar-rSA-ldrtl`; the pass the V6b verification never ran):

    · The old file's two open questions are answered, and the answer was worse than the file
      guessed. The fallback is LEGIBLE, not tofu — but the 126sp clock rendered `12:٤٣`. The
      hour came out in Latin digits and the minutes in Arabic-Indic (observed, on both the old
      and the new build; the mechanism inside WFF's TimeText is not established here, and this
      file does not control it). Lora has Latin digits and no Arabic-Indic ones, so it drew the
      hour and the system fallback drew the minutes: **the face's centrepiece was two typefaces
      at two weights, side by side, in one number.** That is not an Arabic-slots problem, which is
      what the defect had been filed as; it was the clock.
    · The split digits REMAIN — `12:٥٠` after the fix — because they are the platform's
      formatting, not a font choice. What changed is that one typeface now draws both halves, so
      it reads as one number. Worth an owner's eye on whether the mixed system is acceptable;
      nothing in WFF lets this file force one.
    · Noto Naskh carries BOTH Latin and Arabic-Indic digits, so the clock is now self-consistent
      whichever way ICU shapes it. That property is why a font swap fixes this and a locale-
      qualified *layout* would not have.
    · The box heights the file worried about (date_line 26px against a 34.1px Noto line box, and
      the three complication boxes likewise) do NOT clip: WFF lays the text out on its ink, not on
      the hhea line box. Confirmed on screen at ar-SA with the date line, the complication title
      and the "until" line all rendering whole. No geometry moved, so en/tr are pixel-identical —
      also confirmed on the en-US emulator: `Sun, Rabi' I 17 / 12:48 / Isha · 4h 3m` all Lora.

  WHAT IS STILL TRUE AND STILL UNSOLVED — the two-language trap, unchanged by this fix:
  the complication slots take their TEXT from the wear app's envelope (the APP language) while
  these font resources resolve on the SYSTEM locale. So an Arabic-app / English-watch user still
  reads Arabic prayer names in Lora, and an English-app / Arabic-watch user now reads Latin ones
  in Noto Naskh. Both are strictly better than before (one face for the whole dial rather than
  three), and neither is right. Fixing it properly means the envelope carrying its language to the
  face, which WFF gives no mechanism for — a complication provider cannot choose a font. Recorded
  rather than papered over.

  res/font/amiri_regular.ttf (421KB, referenced by nothing) was removed in the same pass.
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
-->
<WatchFace width="450" height="450" clipShape="CIRCLE">
  <Metadata key="CLOCK_TYPE" value="DIGITAL" />
  <Metadata key="PREVIEW_TIME" value="10:08:32" />
  <Scene backgroundColor="#ff050402">

    <!-- Interactive ground: the radial night vignette (pre-rendered PNG; ambient drops it and
         keeps the near-black scene color). -->
    <PartImage x="0" y="0" width="450" height="450" name="ground">
      <Variant mode="AMBIENT" target="alpha" value="0" />
      <Image resource="bg_vellum" />
    </PartImage>

    <!-- The full ring track, rgba(214,180,110,0.25), interactive only. -->
    <PartDraw x="0" y="0" width="450" height="450" name="ring_track">
      <Variant mode="AMBIENT" target="alpha" value="0" />
      <Ellipse x="16" y="16" width="418" height="418">
        <Stroke color="#40d6b46e" thickness="3" />
      </Ellipse>
    </PartDraw>

    <!-- Hijri date + weekday, rendered natively by ICU under the Umm al-Qura calendar:
         "11 Rabiʿ al-Awwal · Mon". (The canvas also shows the Gregorian day-of-month; one
         PartText holds one calendar, so v1 keeps the line fully hijri plus the weekday.) -->
    <!-- 26, not the 20 this shipped with: WFF authors in the declared 450-unit design space and
         the runtime scales it to the display, so on a 192dp watch (WO-V16's floor) 20 arrived as
         8.5dp of type. 26 lands at 11.1dp there and 13.0dp on a 225dp watch. The box grew with
         it — a 26-unit line inside a 26-unit box would clip its own descenders — keeping its
         centre where it was, so nothing else on the face moves. -->
    <PartText x="45" y="88" width="360" height="34" name="date_line">
      <Variant mode="AMBIENT" target="alpha" value="0" />
      <Localization calendar="ISLAMIC_UMALQURA" timeZone="SYNC_TO_DEVICE" />
      <Text align="CENTER" ellipsis="TRUE">
        <Font family="face_regular" size="26" color="#ff9c8a60">
          <Template><![CDATA[%s]]>
            <Parameter expression="icuText(&quot;d MMMM · EEE&quot;)" />
          </Template>
        </Font>
      </Text>
    </PartText>

    <!-- The interactive clock: Lora SemiBold 126, ink, 12/24h following the watch. -->
    <DigitalClock x="25" y="116" width="400" height="140">
      <Variant mode="AMBIENT" target="alpha" value="0" />
      <TimeText x="0" y="0" width="400" height="140" format="h:mm"
        hourFormat="SYNC_TO_DEVICE" align="CENTER">
        <Font family="face_semibold" size="126" color="#ffece0c4" />
      </TimeText>
    </DigitalClock>

    <!-- Ornament: hairline — sujud glyph — hairline (interactive only). -->
    <Group x="130" y="266" width="190" height="20" name="ornament">
      <Variant mode="AMBIENT" target="alpha" value="0" />
      <PartDraw x="0" y="9" width="76" height="2">
        <Rectangle x="0" y="0" width="76" height="1">
          <Fill color="#57d6b46e" />
        </Rectangle>
      </PartDraw>
      <PartImage x="86" y="0" width="19" height="19">
        <Image resource="ornament_sujud" />
      </PartImage>
      <PartDraw x="115" y="9" width="75" height="2">
        <Rectangle x="0" y="0" width="75" height="1">
          <Fill color="#57d6b46e" />
        </Rectangle>
      </PartDraw>
    </Group>

    <!-- The ambient clock: Lora Regular 118, single gold, inside the AOD pixel budget. -->
    <DigitalClock x="25" y="141" width="400" height="132" alpha="0">
      <Variant mode="AMBIENT" target="alpha" value="255" />
      <TimeText x="0" y="0" width="400" height="132" format="h:mm"
        hourFormat="SYNC_TO_DEVICE" align="CENTER">
        <Font family="face_regular" size="118" color="#ffbf9950" />
      </TimeText>
    </DigitalClock>

    <!-- Slot 1 — the next-prayer line, locked to the app's provider. Falls back to the
         system's day-of-week text when the Simple Prayer wear app is not installed. -->
    <ComplicationSlot x="60" y="288" width="330" height="44" slotId="1" name="next_prayer"
      displayName="slot_next_prayer" supportedTypes="SHORT_TEXT" isCustomizable="FALSE">
      <BoundingBox x="0" y="0" width="330" height="44" />
      <DefaultProviderPolicy
        primaryProvider="app.simpleprayer/app.simpleprayer.wear.PrayerComplicationService"
        primaryProviderType="SHORT_TEXT"
        defaultSystemProvider="DAY_OF_WEEK"
        defaultSystemProviderType="SHORT_TEXT" />
      <Complication type="SHORT_TEXT">
        <Condition>
          <Expressions>
            <Expression name="hasTitle"><![CDATA[[COMPLICATION.TITLE] != null]]></Expression>
          </Expressions>
          <Compare expression="hasTitle">
            <!-- Interactive: "Asr · 1:12" in gold Lora SemiBold. -->
            <PartText x="0" y="0" width="330" height="44">
              <Variant mode="AMBIENT" target="alpha" value="0" />
              <Text align="CENTER" ellipsis="TRUE">
                <Font family="face_semibold" size="30" color="#ffdcb96f">
                  <Template><![CDATA[%s · %s]]>
                    <Parameter expression="[COMPLICATION.TITLE]" />
                    <Parameter expression="[COMPLICATION.TEXT]" />
                  </Template>
                </Font>
              </Text>
            </PartText>
            <!-- Ambient: the same fact, one muted gold, smaller. -->
            <PartText x="0" y="6" width="330" height="32" alpha="0">
              <Variant mode="AMBIENT" target="alpha" value="255" />
              <Text align="CENTER" ellipsis="TRUE">
                <Font family="face_regular" size="24" color="#ff93805a">
                  <Template><![CDATA[%s · %s]]>
                    <Parameter expression="[COMPLICATION.TITLE]" />
                    <Parameter expression="[COMPLICATION.TEXT]" />
                  </Template>
                </Font>
              </Text>
            </PartText>
          </Compare>
          <Default>
            <PartText x="0" y="0" width="330" height="44">
              <Variant mode="AMBIENT" target="alpha" value="0" />
              <Text align="CENTER" ellipsis="TRUE">
                <Font family="face_semibold" size="30" color="#ffdcb96f">
                  <Template><![CDATA[%s]]>
                    <Parameter expression="[COMPLICATION.TEXT]" />
                  </Template>
                </Font>
              </Text>
            </PartText>
            <PartText x="0" y="6" width="330" height="32" alpha="0">
              <Variant mode="AMBIENT" target="alpha" value="255" />
              <Text align="CENTER" ellipsis="TRUE">
                <Font family="face_regular" size="24" color="#ff93805a">
                  <Template><![CDATA[%s]]>
                    <Parameter expression="[COMPLICATION.TEXT]" />
                  </Template>
                </Font>
              </Text>
            </PartText>
          </Default>
        </Condition>
      </Complication>
    </ComplicationSlot>

    <!-- Slot 2 — progress through the current prayer window, drawn as the gold arc riding the
         ring track, with the ◆ at the arc's end (the deadline). EMPTY fallback: without the
         app there is no window, so the ring simply stays a quiet track. -->
    <!-- EMPTY sits in supportedTypes because it IS this slot's no-app state (the quiet track);
         the DWF runtime refuses a fallback type missing from the list (device-only check —
         the offline validator passes without it). -->
    <ComplicationSlot x="0" y="0" width="450" height="450" slotId="2" name="prayer_window"
      displayName="slot_prayer_window" supportedTypes="RANGED_VALUE EMPTY" isCustomizable="FALSE">
      <BoundingOval x="0" y="0" width="450" height="450" />
      <DefaultProviderPolicy
        primaryProvider="app.simpleprayer/app.simpleprayer.wear.PrayerComplicationService"
        primaryProviderType="RANGED_VALUE"
        defaultSystemProvider="EMPTY"
        defaultSystemProviderType="EMPTY" />
      <Complication type="RANGED_VALUE">
        <!-- Interactive arc: accent gold, from 12 o'clock, clockwise. -->
        <PartDraw x="0" y="0" width="450" height="450">
          <Variant mode="AMBIENT" target="alpha" value="0" />
          <Arc centerX="225" centerY="225" width="418" height="418"
            startAngle="0" endAngle="0" direction="CLOCKWISE">
            <Stroke color="#ffbf9950" thickness="3" cap="ROUND" />
            <Transform target="endAngle"
              value="(((clamp(([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_VALUE]), ([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_MIN]), ([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_MAX])) - ([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_MIN])) / (([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_MAX]) - ([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_MIN]))) * (360))" />
          </Arc>
        </PartDraw>
        <!-- Ambient arc: thinner, reduced alpha, still the one fact the ring carries. -->
        <PartDraw x="0" y="0" width="450" height="450" alpha="0">
          <Variant mode="AMBIENT" target="alpha" value="255" />
          <Arc centerX="225" centerY="225" width="418" height="418"
            startAngle="0" endAngle="0" direction="CLOCKWISE">
            <Stroke color="#47bf9950" thickness="2" cap="ROUND" />
            <Transform target="endAngle"
              value="(((clamp(([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_VALUE]), ([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_MIN]), ([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_MAX])) - ([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_MIN])) / (([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_MAX]) - ([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_MIN]))) * (360))" />
          </Arc>
        </PartDraw>
        <!-- The ◆ rides the arc's end: this group rotates about the face center by the same
             normalized progress, carrying a 45°-turned square sitting on the ring radius. -->
        <Group x="0" y="0" width="450" height="450" pivotX="0.5" pivotY="0.5" angle="0"
          name="deadline_diamond">
          <Transform target="angle"
            value="(((clamp(([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_VALUE]), ([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_MIN]), ([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_MAX])) - ([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_MIN])) / (([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_MAX]) - ([COMPLICATION.RANGED_VALUE_MIN]))) * (360))" />
          <PartDraw x="217" y="8" width="16" height="16" angle="45">
            <Variant mode="AMBIENT" target="alpha" value="0" />
            <Rectangle x="2.5" y="2.5" width="11" height="11">
              <Fill color="#ffcba85e" />
            </Rectangle>
          </PartDraw>
          <PartDraw x="217" y="8" width="16" height="16" angle="45" alpha="0">
            <Variant mode="AMBIENT" target="alpha" value="255" />
            <Rectangle x="3.5" y="3.5" width="9" height="9">
              <Fill color="#b3cba85e" />
            </Rectangle>
          </PartDraw>
        </Group>
        <!-- "until 6:42 pm" — rendered only if the provider fills the ranged complication's
             text field; the face loses nothing when it is absent. Interactive only. -->
        <Condition>
          <Expressions>
            <Expression name="hasUntil"><![CDATA[[COMPLICATION.TEXT] != null]]></Expression>
          </Expressions>
          <Compare expression="hasUntil">
            <!-- 26 and a box grown to match, for the same reason as the date line above: 20
                 reached a 192dp wrist as 8.5dp. Centre unchanged. -->
            <PartText x="105" y="330" width="240" height="34">
              <Variant mode="AMBIENT" target="alpha" value="0" />
              <Text align="CENTER" ellipsis="TRUE">
                <Font family="face_regular" size="26" color="#ffad9a6e">
                  <Template><![CDATA[%s]]>
                    <Parameter expression="[COMPLICATION.TEXT]" />
                  </Template>
                </Font>
              </Text>
            </PartText>
          </Compare>
        </Condition>
      </Complication>
    </ComplicationSlot>
  </Scene>
</WatchFace>
